Z||000003||batboy||10-15-2000||10:23 PM||||Number one, it's not all that easy and number two, a V6 going into a 84 is especially a pain with the different wiring harness and with the bulkhead in a different location. You'll need the donor car's ECM (computer) and all the wiring from there to the engine. You'll also need the donor car's motor mounts and dog bone. You'll need to use the V6 exhaust and fuel pump too I believe. Plus lots of little crap that I'm forgetting.||||reg||1
